WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.127
- We took a lot of pride in trailblazing,

00:00:03.127 --> 00:00:04.639
and how the game was played.

00:00:04.639 --> 00:00:06.464
I knew at that time, when I was eight,

00:00:06.464 --> 00:00:08.216
I wanted to be an entertainer.

00:00:08.216 --> 00:00:09.776
And I loved the idea of that.

00:00:09.776 --> 00:00:12.496
It wasn't me, personally,
that they didn't like.

00:00:12.496 --> 00:00:15.669
It was that I wasn't being me.

00:00:15.669 --> 00:00:17.099
Life brings drama,

00:00:17.099 --> 00:00:18.557
and you've got to deal with this person,

00:00:18.557 --> 00:00:20.254
and maintain a healthy relationship.

00:00:20.254 --> 00:00:21.446
Yes, I get up at crazy hours,

00:00:21.446 --> 00:00:23.015
whether it's three o'clock in the morning.

00:00:23.015 --> 00:00:24.713
By the way, when we
were talking in London,

00:00:24.713 --> 00:00:25.603
I was getting up at three

00:00:25.603 --> 00:00:26.885
'cause I had to be on set at four.

00:00:26.885 --> 00:00:29.148
It is the worst mistake
you will ever make.

00:00:29.148 --> 00:00:31.912
He said, "You're ruining your career."

00:00:31.912 --> 00:00:34.224
I love action, and I love kickin' ass.

00:00:34.224 --> 00:00:36.733
But the goal is to become a better actor.

00:00:36.733 --> 00:00:38.127
Get your ass kicked, get back up,

00:00:38.127 --> 00:00:40.778
and put the gloves back
on, and you swing away.

00:00:40.778 --> 00:00:43.031
When I was 16 years old,

00:00:43.031 --> 00:00:44.758
that was the last time
that I was arrested.

00:00:44.758 --> 00:00:46.013
I don't know how it happened,

00:00:46.013 --> 00:00:48.363
but my cousin, who was on tour with us,

00:00:48.363 --> 00:00:50.756
actually just got busted with prostitutes,

00:00:50.756 --> 00:00:53.115
and my name is attached to it now.

00:00:53.115 --> 00:00:55.784
- He's a Canadian-American
actor, producer,

00:00:55.784 --> 00:00:57.805
and semi-retired wrestler.

00:00:57.805 --> 00:01:00.836
The Rock is considered by many
to be the biggest superstar

00:01:00.836 --> 00:01:02.865
in WWE history.

00:01:02.865 --> 00:01:06.600
His autobiography debuted
at #1 on the New York Times

00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:07.896
Bestseller List.

00:01:07.896 --> 00:01:09.317
He's Dwayne 'The Rock' Johnson,

00:01:09.317 --> 00:01:12.817
and here are his top 10 rules for success.

00:01:15.202 --> 00:01:16.035
- We were bad.

00:01:16.035 --> 00:01:17.079
We intimidated, we dominated,

00:01:17.079 --> 00:01:18.849
but we took a lot of pride in that!

00:01:18.849 --> 00:01:21.422
We took a lot of pride in trailblazing,

00:01:21.422 --> 00:01:23.941
and how the game was
played back at that time.

00:01:23.941 --> 00:01:26.583
We would intimidate teams,

00:01:26.583 --> 00:01:28.447
and we would want to dominate teams.

00:01:28.447 --> 00:01:30.392
But also, too, we also
had the thought process

00:01:30.392 --> 00:01:32.418
that a team was never going to outwork us.

00:01:32.418 --> 00:01:34.390
We were going to be the hardest
working team in the country.

00:01:34.390 --> 00:01:35.328
And check this out.

00:01:35.328 --> 00:01:36.286
What we would do, for example,

00:01:36.286 --> 00:01:40.034
we would have a big game
that has a lot at stake.

00:01:40.034 --> 00:01:42.348
So we would go into the
Doak Campbell Stadium,

00:01:42.348 --> 00:01:44.788
and instead of going through
your general practice,

00:01:44.788 --> 00:01:48.167
what we would do is do things
a little bit different,

00:01:48.167 --> 00:01:49.255
just to intimidate them.

00:01:49.255 --> 00:01:52.224
So as a team, we would
kind of all line up,

00:01:52.224 --> 00:01:54.206
we're in their stadium,
we've got their staff,

00:01:54.206 --> 00:01:55.357
we've got some players
who are watching us.

00:01:55.357 --> 00:01:56.385
Instead of going through our plays,

00:01:56.385 --> 00:01:58.903
we would just start to give cadence calls.

00:01:58.903 --> 00:02:01.397
So, for example, the whole team,

00:02:01.397 --> 00:02:03.564
we would say things like--

00:02:06.168 --> 00:02:07.614
- I don't know, maybe you scared them!

00:02:07.614 --> 00:02:09.210
(Dwayne laughs)

00:02:09.210 --> 00:02:10.229
Don't hold back, Dwayne!

00:02:10.229 --> 00:02:13.263
- We would say, "All us
Canes, we got an itch!

00:02:13.263 --> 00:02:15.876
"Florida State's going to be our bitch!"

00:02:15.876 --> 00:02:17.331
(audience laughs and cheers)

00:02:17.331 --> 00:02:18.283
Like that!

00:02:18.283 --> 00:02:19.119
I wanted to entertain.

00:02:19.119 --> 00:02:21.052
When I was eight years old,
I thought I was a combination

00:02:21.052 --> 00:02:21.892
of these guys.

00:02:21.892 --> 00:02:24.041
I thought I was a
combination of Chuck Norris,

00:02:24.041 --> 00:02:28.649
Richard Pryor, Harrison
Ford, and Rocky Balboa.

00:02:28.649 --> 00:02:30.262
And Harrison Ford from Indiana Jones.

00:02:30.262 --> 00:02:33.367
So I was like all these
guys, and Elvis Presley, too.

00:02:33.367 --> 00:02:35.217
Yeah, eight, right? (laughs)

00:02:35.217 --> 00:02:36.467
- [Announcer] Lofty
ambitions, right? (laughs)

00:02:36.467 --> 00:02:40.822
- So I knew at that
time, when I was eight,

00:02:40.822 --> 00:02:42.838
I wanted to be an entertainer,

00:02:42.838 --> 00:02:44.175
and I loved the idea of that,

00:02:44.175 --> 00:02:45.008
and what it meant.

00:02:45.008 --> 00:02:46.125
And when I was eight,

00:02:46.125 --> 00:02:48.228
I saw Indiana Jones for the first time,

00:02:48.228 --> 00:02:49.864
and I love that character.

00:02:49.864 --> 00:02:53.073
I'm like, wow, that guy was
so heroic, he kicked ass.

00:02:53.073 --> 00:02:56.406
I remember I had great angst every night

00:02:57.976 --> 00:03:01.304
before I went out, because
I was not able to be myself.

00:03:01.304 --> 00:03:03.767
(announcers shouting)

00:03:03.767 --> 00:03:07.938
(audience cheering loudly)

00:03:07.938 --> 00:03:10.566
My very first Wrestlemania,
the biggest show of the year,

00:03:10.566 --> 00:03:12.816
the Superbowl of wrestling.

00:03:15.251 --> 00:03:18.924
That night, 20,000 fans started
chanting, "Rocky sucks!"

00:03:18.924 --> 00:03:22.364
(laughs) It was a sobering moment.

00:03:22.364 --> 00:03:24.322
And that was the beginning of the end

00:03:24.322 --> 00:03:26.739
of my initial run in the WWE.

00:03:28.970 --> 00:03:31.886
A few weeks later, I
tore a tendon in my knee,

00:03:31.886 --> 00:03:34.775
and I was out for the rest of the summer.

00:03:34.775 --> 00:03:36.587
I came to the realization
before I went back

00:03:36.587 --> 00:03:40.463
that it wasn't me, personally,
that they didn't like.

00:03:40.463 --> 00:03:42.963
It was that I wasn't being me.

00:03:44.153 --> 00:03:47.570
I wasn't being real,
wasn't being authentic.

00:03:47.570 --> 00:03:49.569
Who is this guy, in
wrestling, who's smiling

00:03:49.569 --> 00:03:51.805
when he's getting beat?

00:03:51.805 --> 00:03:54.792
A few weeks later, I
got a call from the WWE,

00:03:54.792 --> 00:03:56.547
and I spoke to Vince McMahon.

00:03:56.547 --> 00:03:58.923
He said, "When you come
back, we could continue

00:03:58.923 --> 00:04:01.175
"to shove you down people's throats,

00:04:01.175 --> 00:04:04.583
"or we could your heel because
they want to boo you anyway."

00:04:04.583 --> 00:04:06.496
I said, "It's a great idea."

00:04:06.496 --> 00:04:08.688
And I said, "Before we get off the phone,

00:04:08.688 --> 00:04:10.091
"I have one request."

00:04:10.091 --> 00:04:12.581
I said, "When I come back, and we go live,

00:04:12.581 --> 00:04:15.081
"I just need two minutes live.

00:04:16.770 --> 00:04:19.762
"Me, talking to the audience, live.

00:04:19.762 --> 00:04:21.639
"Two minutes is all I'm asking."

00:04:21.639 --> 00:04:23.913
He said, "Okay, you got it."

00:04:23.913 --> 00:04:26.314
Couple weeks later, I came
back, we were on live TV,

00:04:26.314 --> 00:04:30.383
I grabbed the microphone,
fans were already booing.

00:04:30.383 --> 00:04:32.138
They started chanting, "Rocky sucks".

00:04:32.138 --> 00:04:34.214
In arenas across the country,

00:04:34.214 --> 00:04:36.964
I heard chants of "Rocky sucks".

00:04:36.964 --> 00:04:39.440
(audience cheers)

00:04:39.440 --> 00:04:42.273
I said, "I may be a lot of things,

00:04:43.859 --> 00:04:46.653
"The Rocky might seem
like a lot of things,

00:04:46.653 --> 00:04:48.854
"But 'sucks' isn't one of them."

00:04:48.854 --> 00:04:51.044
But 'sucks' isn't one of 'em!

00:04:51.044 --> 00:04:53.877
In that moment, The Rock was born.

00:04:56.817 --> 00:04:58.817
And about a month later,

00:05:00.190 --> 00:05:03.241
I was the hottest deal in the company.

00:05:03.241 --> 00:05:05.334
(pensive music)

00:05:05.334 --> 00:05:07.334
And things were on fire.

00:05:08.720 --> 00:05:12.762
And the greatest lesson
about that is, be you.

00:05:12.762 --> 00:05:17.177
Be yourself, whether
it's in entertainment,

00:05:17.177 --> 00:05:19.427
whether it's out in public,

00:05:21.142 --> 00:05:24.869
whether you're a celebrity
or not, whatever.

00:05:24.869 --> 00:05:27.537
The most powerful thing
you could be is yourself.

00:05:27.537 --> 00:05:30.015
Yes, I get up super early, generally.

00:05:30.015 --> 00:05:32.378
I have this thing where I
like beating the sun up.

00:05:32.378 --> 00:05:35.611
If the sun is down, I have to get up.

00:05:35.611 --> 00:05:37.194
And how do I do it?

00:05:38.355 --> 00:05:40.420
It's just important to find balance,

00:05:40.420 --> 00:05:44.583
and I try to do things
that I really enjoy doing.

00:05:44.583 --> 00:05:47.308
And a lot of the times, it's like in life,

00:05:47.308 --> 00:05:50.456
life brings drama and you
have to deal with this person,

00:05:50.456 --> 00:05:52.615
and then have a healthy relationship here,

00:05:52.615 --> 00:05:53.815
and all these things.

00:05:53.815 --> 00:05:56.576
You try just to kind of balance
them out as best as I can.

00:05:56.576 --> 00:05:58.488
I have a great team around me, by the way,

00:05:58.488 --> 00:06:02.217
who really, really helps
me, allows for me to come in

00:06:02.217 --> 00:06:05.025
and work 12 hours a day, 14 hours a day.

00:06:05.025 --> 00:06:06.478
Get up at three o'clock in the morning,

00:06:06.478 --> 00:06:09.249
send out an Instagram
video where I'm talking

00:06:09.249 --> 00:06:11.553
to my cardio machine like a crazy maniac.

00:06:11.553 --> 00:06:12.653
(audience laughs)

00:06:12.653 --> 00:06:14.184
Yeah, requires a lot of people around.

00:06:14.184 --> 00:06:16.232
Yes, I get up at crazy hours,

00:06:16.232 --> 00:06:17.781
whether it's three o'clock in the morning.

00:06:17.781 --> 00:06:19.378
By the way, when we
were talking in London,

00:06:19.378 --> 00:06:21.477
I was getting up at three 'cause
I had to be on set by four.

00:06:21.477 --> 00:06:23.038
I'm sorry, by seven.

00:06:23.038 --> 00:06:26.165
So whatever time my
call-time is, and I tell this

00:06:26.165 --> 00:06:29.667
to studios and directors and producers.

00:06:29.667 --> 00:06:33.834
So my call-time is at seven,
then you back your clock up

00:06:34.739 --> 00:06:36.687
four hours and then that's when I get up,

00:06:36.687 --> 00:06:37.896
and I train twice.

00:06:37.896 --> 00:06:39.094
I get my cardio in, breakfast,

00:06:39.094 --> 00:06:40.594
and then I'll go hit the weights.

00:06:40.594 --> 00:06:44.381
Clangin' and bangin', we
call it. Jackin' iron!

00:06:44.381 --> 00:06:46.699
- But like, what time do you go to bed?

00:06:46.699 --> 00:06:48.761
You might shoot really late at night.

00:06:48.761 --> 00:06:52.702
- On a movie, I probably average
about five hours of sleep.

00:06:52.702 --> 00:06:54.301
I found that with depression,

00:06:54.301 --> 00:06:57.211
one of the most important
things you could realize

00:06:57.211 --> 00:06:58.395
is that you're not alone.

00:06:58.395 --> 00:07:00.371
You're not the first to go through it,

00:07:00.371 --> 00:07:01.986
you're not going to be
the last to go through it.

00:07:01.986 --> 00:07:03.521
And oftentimes, it happens.

00:07:03.521 --> 00:07:07.211
You feel like you're alone, and
you feel like it's only you,

00:07:07.211 --> 00:07:11.150
and you're in your bubble,
and I wish I had someone

00:07:11.150 --> 00:07:15.067
at that time who could
just pull me aside, and,

00:07:19.082 --> 00:07:21.677
"Hey, it's going to be
okay. It'll be okay."

00:07:21.677 --> 00:07:24.425
I wish I knew that, you've
just got to remember,

00:07:24.425 --> 00:07:28.175
hold on to that fundamental
quality of faith.

00:07:29.590 --> 00:07:33.450
Have faith, and on the
other side of your pain

00:07:33.450 --> 00:07:34.950
is something good.

00:07:37.888 --> 00:07:41.305
After about a month and a half of staying

00:07:42.654 --> 00:07:44.728
in that little apartment and cleaning,

00:07:44.728 --> 00:07:47.651
I got a phone call from
the head coach of the team

00:07:47.651 --> 00:07:48.953
who cut me.

00:07:48.953 --> 00:07:50.659
Head coach of the Calgary Stampeders.

00:07:50.659 --> 00:07:52.527
He called me and he said,
"Hey, I know we cut you,

00:07:52.527 --> 00:07:53.909
"but I'd like you to come back."

00:07:53.909 --> 00:07:55.837
I said, "Okay, I appreciate that, Coach.

00:07:55.837 --> 00:07:57.937
"Thank you very much,
I'll think about it."

00:07:57.937 --> 00:07:58.770
And he said, "Okay, great."

00:07:58.770 --> 00:08:00.975
I hung up the phone, and my dad said,

00:08:00.975 --> 00:08:02.282
"You're going to do it, right?"

00:08:02.282 --> 00:08:05.601
I said, "No, I don't think so.

00:08:05.601 --> 00:08:07.972
"I think I'm done with that."

00:08:07.972 --> 00:08:09.538
And he goes, "What?"

00:08:09.538 --> 00:08:12.199
I said, "My gut tells me I'm done."

00:08:12.199 --> 00:08:14.146
He said, "What are you going to do?"

00:08:14.146 --> 00:08:15.896
I took a deep breath,

00:08:17.277 --> 00:08:19.936
I said that I'd like to
get into the business.

00:08:19.936 --> 00:08:21.393
He said, "What business?"

00:08:21.393 --> 00:08:22.756
I said, "The wrestling business."

00:08:22.756 --> 00:08:26.347
He said, "You are throwing it all away.

00:08:26.347 --> 00:08:29.792
"It is the worst mistake
you will ever make."

00:08:29.792 --> 00:08:33.349
He said, "You're ruining your career."

00:08:33.349 --> 00:08:37.266
I said, "Maybe I'll be
no good, but I feel like

00:08:38.407 --> 00:08:40.220
"in my heart, I have to do this,

00:08:40.220 --> 00:08:43.053
"and I either need you to train me

00:08:46.691 --> 00:08:49.358
"or I need you to not train me."

00:08:50.940 --> 00:08:54.628
My dad rose to the occasion, so I trained.

00:08:54.628 --> 00:08:58.287
And it wound up being one
of the greatest chapters

00:08:58.287 --> 00:08:59.204
in my life.

00:09:00.393 --> 00:09:02.044
The goal, and this is
my 10th year of acting,

00:09:02.044 --> 00:09:03.307
the goal is always to work,

00:09:03.307 --> 00:09:04.699
and I started in the action genre.

00:09:04.699 --> 00:09:06.853
I love action, and I love kickin' ass.

00:09:06.853 --> 00:09:08.730
But the goal is to become a better actor,

00:09:08.730 --> 00:09:11.636
and so, for me, in
order for me to do that,

00:09:11.636 --> 00:09:13.178
I had to work in all different genres.

00:09:13.178 --> 00:09:16.030
I wanted to explore
family movies, comedies,

00:09:16.030 --> 00:09:20.267
action-comedies, family comedies,
mix drama into it as well.

00:09:20.267 --> 00:09:23.060
So that was important to
me, just to get better.

00:09:23.060 --> 00:09:24.708
I knew I wanted to be something,

00:09:24.708 --> 00:09:26.329
and it was important
to me to be something.

00:09:26.329 --> 00:09:29.238
It was important to me that I didn't fail.

00:09:29.238 --> 00:09:32.448
By the way, if I did fail,
what was also important

00:09:32.448 --> 00:09:33.407
was the lesson.

00:09:33.407 --> 00:09:36.087
And I didn't realize
that until I got older.

00:09:36.087 --> 00:09:38.334
'Cause when you're in
it, you're in the grind,

00:09:38.334 --> 00:09:40.224
you don't really recognize those things

00:09:40.224 --> 00:09:43.163
when you're younger, but
I can recognize them now,

00:09:43.163 --> 00:09:44.414
and the importance of them now.

00:09:44.414 --> 00:09:46.249
And in terms of the drive
and the determination,

00:09:46.249 --> 00:09:48.916
a lot of it was experience, too.

00:09:49.944 --> 00:09:51.904
Get your ass kicked, get back up,

00:09:51.904 --> 00:09:55.109
put the gloves back
on, and you swing away.

00:09:55.109 --> 00:09:57.646
When I was 16 years old,

00:09:57.646 --> 00:09:59.198
that was the last time
that I was arrested,

00:09:59.198 --> 00:10:02.502
and at that time, we
were at an all-time low,

00:10:02.502 --> 00:10:04.036
I think, with our family.

00:10:04.036 --> 00:10:06.527
At that time, we were living
in Bethlehem, Pennsylvania.

00:10:06.527 --> 00:10:10.277
And I am already a pretty
big boy, 6'4", 200,

00:10:11.307 --> 00:10:13.747
maybe 225 pounds, I had
a very bad mustache.

00:10:13.747 --> 00:10:16.228
I had a chip on my shoulder.

00:10:16.228 --> 00:10:20.378
Fresh into this high school
in Bethlehem, Pennsylvania,

00:10:20.378 --> 00:10:21.576
Freedom High School.

00:10:21.576 --> 00:10:23.260
I wanted to use the bathroom,

00:10:23.260 --> 00:10:25.099
but I didn't want to use
the regular boys' bathroom,

00:10:25.099 --> 00:10:27.329
because the boys' bathroom
smelled like smoke,

00:10:27.329 --> 00:10:31.066
and all the other fun stuff
that boys' bathrooms smell like.

00:10:31.066 --> 00:10:32.433
So I ended up going into
the teacher's lounge,

00:10:32.433 --> 00:10:37.371
and a teacher comes in, his
name is Jody Swick, tough guy.

00:10:37.371 --> 00:10:40.478
He says, "Hey, you can't be in here!"

00:10:40.478 --> 00:10:43.561
I kind of pause, look over my shoulder,

00:10:44.859 --> 00:10:47.609
"Okay, I'll leave when I'm done."

00:10:48.804 --> 00:10:51.422
And I continued to wash my hands.

00:10:51.422 --> 00:10:55.025
I slowly dried my hands,
and I walked by him,

00:10:55.025 --> 00:10:57.740
and I kind of just looked
at 'em as I walked by,

00:10:57.740 --> 00:11:00.573
he looked at me, didn't say
a word, but he was fuming.

00:11:00.573 --> 00:11:02.712
I went home that night and I felt bad.

00:11:02.712 --> 00:11:04.045
I just felt bad.

00:11:04.948 --> 00:11:08.112
The very next day, I found him,

00:11:08.112 --> 00:11:11.317
and I went to see him in
his class, and I said,

00:11:11.317 --> 00:11:15.484
"I just want to apologize
for how I acted yesterday,

00:11:17.110 --> 00:11:18.443
"and I'm sorry."

00:11:20.860 --> 00:11:22.759
And I stuck my hand out.

00:11:22.759 --> 00:11:24.356
And he looked at my
hand, and looked at me,

00:11:24.356 --> 00:11:25.729
and he looked at my hand again.

00:11:25.729 --> 00:11:29.820
And he shook my hand. I'll
never forget that shake.

00:11:29.820 --> 00:11:31.403
He wouldn't let go.

00:11:32.505 --> 00:11:35.863
He said, "I want you to
do something for me."

00:11:35.863 --> 00:11:37.596
I said, "Yes?"

00:11:37.596 --> 00:11:39.439
And he said, "Why don't you come out

00:11:39.439 --> 00:11:40.815
"and play football for me?"

00:11:40.815 --> 00:11:42.065
I said, "Okay."

00:11:43.055 --> 00:11:45.549
He said, "Alright, I have your word?"

00:11:45.549 --> 00:11:47.818
"Yeah, sure, you've got my word."

00:11:47.818 --> 00:11:49.538
I didn't think much of it,

00:11:49.538 --> 00:11:51.743
I thought, okay, I'll play some football.

00:11:51.743 --> 00:11:54.551
I like playing football, it's cool.

00:11:54.551 --> 00:11:58.949
And I went out, and I played
football for Jody Swick,

00:11:58.949 --> 00:12:00.897
and he was our head football coach,

00:12:00.897 --> 00:12:05.064
and he became a father
figure to me, and a mentor.

00:12:07.627 --> 00:12:09.443
I fell in love with the game of football.

00:12:09.443 --> 00:12:12.794
My grades got better, and
I started getting recruited

00:12:12.794 --> 00:12:15.319
from every college across the country.

00:12:15.319 --> 00:12:18.504
College coaches would come in and say,

00:12:18.504 --> 00:12:21.837
"There he is, Dwayne Johnson, 6'4", 250.

00:12:22.965 --> 00:12:26.891
"Plays both sides of the
ball, very aggressive."

00:12:26.891 --> 00:12:28.789
My thought process started to change.

00:12:28.789 --> 00:12:30.778
That's when I started
thinking about goals,

00:12:30.778 --> 00:12:32.379
and what I wanted to accomplish.

00:12:32.379 --> 00:12:33.925
And I love that man.

00:12:33.925 --> 00:12:36.782
I'll never forget the impact
that he had in my life,

00:12:36.782 --> 00:12:40.293
and the reminder that I might take away

00:12:40.293 --> 00:12:42.489
from that amazing relationship that I had

00:12:42.489 --> 00:12:45.989
was the empathy that he had for a punk kid

00:12:47.258 --> 00:12:51.091
who treated him so rudely
and disrespectfully.

00:12:52.060 --> 00:12:54.977
He looked past that B.S., and said,

00:12:56.546 --> 00:13:00.097
"I believe in you, and I
want to turn you around."

00:13:00.097 --> 00:13:01.903
Oftentimes, when I see kids,

00:13:01.903 --> 00:13:04.394
and they have been labeled,
"Oh, they're punk kids."

00:13:04.394 --> 00:13:06.894
True, but there's good in 'em,

00:13:09.494 --> 00:13:11.857
and we've got to see that potential.

00:13:11.857 --> 00:13:13.845
And I enjoy that today,
seeing the potential in kids,

00:13:13.845 --> 00:13:15.270
just like he did.

00:13:15.270 --> 00:13:17.773
Especially kids who are kind of wayward.

00:13:17.773 --> 00:13:19.352
And they've been going through it.

00:13:19.352 --> 00:13:22.852
I know what it's like, so thank you, Jody.

00:13:24.166 --> 00:13:25.583
Thank you, buddy.

00:13:27.833 --> 00:13:29.638
I love April Fool's, but
the thing about it is,

00:13:29.638 --> 00:13:32.937
my April Fool's runs the entire year.

00:13:32.937 --> 00:13:37.058
Because it's like, April
Fool's, everyone's expecting it.

00:13:37.058 --> 00:13:39.249
So there's past around Christmastime,

00:13:39.249 --> 00:13:41.102
when we're getting ready
to make a big announcement

00:13:41.102 --> 00:13:44.575
for a movie, and I called
my agent, I was overseas,

00:13:44.575 --> 00:13:46.065
and I called my agent, Brad Slater.

00:13:46.065 --> 00:13:47.251
I woke him up in the middle of the night,

00:13:47.251 --> 00:13:49.067
and I was like, "Hey man,
I got to talk to you."

00:13:49.067 --> 00:13:50.312
He was like, "What's
going on, what's wrong?"

00:13:50.312 --> 00:13:51.917
I said, "I don't know how it happened,

00:13:51.917 --> 00:13:54.440
"but my cousin, who's on tour with us,

00:13:54.440 --> 00:13:56.364
"just got busted with prostitutes,

00:13:56.364 --> 00:13:58.760
"and my name is attached to it now,

00:13:58.760 --> 00:14:01.420
"and it's all getting
ready to hit the press."

00:14:01.420 --> 00:14:02.961
He started freaking out.

00:14:02.961 --> 00:14:04.172
I was like, "Brad, are you okay?"

00:14:04.172 --> 00:14:05.394
He's getting emotional.

00:14:05.394 --> 00:14:06.776
"Oh my god, what are we going to do?"

00:14:06.776 --> 00:14:09.553
And he goes, "I'm going
to be calm in the pocket,

00:14:09.553 --> 00:14:11.147
"I'm thinkin' about this, hold on."

00:14:11.147 --> 00:14:12.256
And I was like, "I don't know what to do.

00:14:12.256 --> 00:14:14.326
"There's like, multiple
prostitutes with this thing."

00:14:14.326 --> 00:14:15.335
(audience laughs)

00:14:15.335 --> 00:14:17.381
"There's a whole ring over
here, and it's unbelievable!"

00:14:17.381 --> 00:14:19.740
I had him going and going,
and finally, I was like,

00:14:19.740 --> 00:14:21.001
"Oh, Brad!" And he was like, "What?"

00:14:21.001 --> 00:14:22.501
"December Fools'!"

00:14:23.587 --> 00:14:26.719
(audience laughs and applauds)

00:14:26.719 --> 00:14:29.386
(Dwayne laughs)

00:14:30.855 --> 00:14:31.724
- [Announcer] That's ridiculous!

00:14:31.724 --> 00:14:34.798
- And that's the thing, I'm
like, "December Fools'!"

00:14:34.798 --> 00:14:36.346
You've got to say it like that,

00:14:36.346 --> 00:14:38.128
and there was a long pause.

00:14:38.128 --> 00:14:39.084
- Thank you so much for watching,

00:14:39.084 --> 00:14:41.655
I made this video because
David Uyan asked me to,

00:14:41.655 --> 00:14:43.302
so if there's a famous entrepreneur

00:14:43.302 --> 00:14:44.687
that you want me to profile next,

00:14:44.687 --> 00:14:46.909
leave it in the comments below
and I'll see what I can do.

00:14:46.909 --> 00:14:50.223
I also love to know which
of The Rock's top 10 tips

00:14:50.223 --> 00:14:51.467
meant the most to you,

00:14:51.467 --> 00:14:53.363
is going to have the biggest
impact on your life and business?

00:14:53.363 --> 00:14:55.600
Leave it in the comments,
and join the discussion.

00:14:55.600 --> 00:14:58.161
Thank you so much for
watching, continue to believe,

00:14:58.161 --> 00:14:59.629
and I'll see you soon.

00:14:59.629 --> 00:15:01.879
(swooping)

